      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate ${∬}_{D}3x{e}^{y}\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over the type I region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}3x{e}^{y}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}3x{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}3x{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{e}^{y}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x{[{e}^{y}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-{e}^{0})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3x(x-1)dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{2}-3x)dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(3{x}^{2}-3x)dx & ={[{x}^{3}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =(64-24)-(1-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =40+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{81}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
